        "content": "<p>jrandolf opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14835\">PR #14835</a> from <code>jrandolf:map-lift-validate-before-alloc</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Lifting a <code>map&lt;K, V&gt;</code> into a <code>HashMap</code> reserved capacity for the guest-supplied length before checking that the entries actually fit in linear memory. This moves the allocation after the bounds, alignment and fuel checks, the same order lists use.</p>\n<p>For reference, before this change a guest with a single page of memory returning <code>(ptr = 0, len = u32::MAX)</code> for a <code>map&lt;u32, u32&gt;</code> made the host's peak RSS jump by about 8 GiB (hashbrown initializes its control bytes) before the call failed with the bounds error. The added test checks for that error; I couldn't find a non-flaky way to assert on the allocation itself, but I'm happy to add one if there's a preferred pattern.</p>\n<p>Closes #14810<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633108433,
